Question ID: GEO_U04_L07_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.GEO.TRI.5
Question:
A support beam forms a right triangle with legs 9 ft and 12 ft. What is the hypotenuse length?
{
~A. 21 ft#Adding the legs does not find the hypotenuse.
~B. 3 ft#Subtracting the legs does not find the hypotenuse.
~C. 108 ft#Multiplying the legs does not find a side length.
=D. 15 ft#Use the Pythagorean Theorem; the hypotenuse is 15 ft.
}
