::GEO_U04_L07_Q06::
Question ID: GEO_U04_L07_Q06
MLA Standard: MLA.GEO.TRI.5
Question:
A ladder is the hypotenuse of length 13 ft, and one leg is 5 ft. What is the other leg?
{
=A. 12 ft#Use b? = 13? - 5?; the missing leg is 12 ft.
~B. 8 ft#Subtracting side lengths ignores the squared relationship.
~C. 18 ft#Adding lengths does not solve for a missing leg.
~D. sqrt(194) ft#This adds squares even though the hypotenuse is already known.
}
